{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011aPVaYVJNTbE3UW8CMzqR9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The `review` service is fully implemented and verified. Everything builds, vets clean, and all pre-existing tests pass.\n\n## What I produced\n\n**gRPC contract** — `proto/v1/review.proto`: package `review.v1`, `go_package = ...;reviewv1`, service `ReviewService` with exactly the three RPCs from the spec (`PostReview`, `ListReviews`, `GetAggregate`) and request/response messages matching the spec shapes (plus the `Review` message used by `ListReviews`).\n\n**Go service**\n- `internal/server/server.go` — in-memory store (`map[hotel_id][]*Review` in post order, mutex-guarded). Handlers implement the described behavior and the `error_semantics` codes:\n  - `PostReview` → `InvalidArgument` when `hotel_id`/`user_id` empty or `rating` outside [1,5].\n  - `ListReviews` → `InvalidArgument` when `page`/`page_size` non-positive; 1-based paging; unknown hotel → empty page, `total_count` 0.\n  - `GetAggregate` → synchronous count + mean; no reviews → (0, 0).\n- `cmd/review/main.go` — gRPC on `:50051`, HTTP `/healthz` (200) on `:8080`, stdlib `log`, SIGTERM graceful shutdown, and a `//go:generate protoc ...` directive.\n\n**Build/deploy** — `Makefile` (`build`/`test`/`image`, leaf-service `image` = `docker build -t agentbench/review:dev .`), multi-stage `Dockerfile` → `gcr.io/distroless/static-debian12` exposing `50051`/`8080`. `go.mod`/`go.sum` tidied (only third-party requires — grpc, protobuf).\n\n## Notes\n- **Leaf service** (`dependent_interface: []`) — no cross-service imports, no `replace` directives, Dockerfile builds from the service dir and never copies `go.work`.\n- The root `go.work` lists sibling services that don't yet exist (no `go.mod`), which breaks *plain* `go` invocations across the whole workspace — a pre-existing environment artifact, not something in `review`. My module is self-contained: it build